0">How To Install Jupyter Notebook on Mac and Windows</h1><p class=3D"gamut=
-1dzl6xd-StyledText e8i0p5k0"><span data-testid=3D"markdown" class=3D"style=
s_markdown__Y5HHD gamut-1leh7be-MarkdownWrapper-spacingNone e1mjarmv0" spac=
ing=3D"none">Learn to install Jupyter Notebook on Mac and Windows using Ana=
conda and  Miniconda. Follow this step-by-step guide for a seamless Jupyter=
 Notebook setup.</span></p><div class=3D"gamut-b63km8-Box e164dx5n1"><div d=
ata-testid=3D"markdown" class=3D"styles_markdown__Y5HHD styles_darkTheme__s=
fPfQ e164dx5n0 gamut-1mhtesm-MarkdownWrapper-markdownStyle-spacingLoose e1m=
jarmv0" spacing=3D"loose"><p class=3D"g-md-p">We recommend installing Jupyt=
er Notebook as part of either <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.anac=
onda.com/products/individual" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14v=
pv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Anaconda</a> or as an addition to <a target=3D"_bla=
nk" href=3D"https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/miniconda.html" class=3D"g-md-a=
 gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Miniconda</a>. Jupyte=
r Notebook can be installed separately, but having either Anaconda or Minic=
onda already installed makes installing Jupyter Notebook easier. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Chromebook users</strong>=
, please see <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/articl=
es/jupyter-notebook-chromebook" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e1=
4vpv2g0">this article</a> because the installation process is slightly diff=
erent.</p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-what-is-anaconda-conda-and-miniconda" class=3D"g-md-h2">W=
hat is Anaconda, Conda, and Miniconda?</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Anaconda is a Python and R distribution that comes with=
 all the tools you need to start working with data, including packages, dev=
elopment environments, and more. However, it requires a lot of memory (3 GB=
). Miniconda is a =E2=80=9Cminimal=E2=80=9D version of Anaconda that requir=
es less memory (about 50 MB) but does not come with any packages or environ=
ments pre-installed. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Both Anaconda and Miniconda come with conda. Conda is a=
 package manager. Package managers help with installing, updating, and remo=
ving packages. <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/reso=
urces/docs/python/pip" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">=
Pip</a> is another popular package manager, and we will use both. The diffe=
rence between conda and pip is that conda manages packages and environments=
 in any language (including Python), whereas pip only manages Python packag=
es. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">We will use pip to manage Python packages since it is t=
he method recommended by the <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.pypa.=
io/en/latest/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"n=
oopener">Python Packaging Authority</a>. Conda=E2=80=99s role in our workfl=
ow is to manage Jupyter Notebook. </p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-anaconda-vs-miniconda-which-one-to-install-for-jupyter-no=
tebook" class=3D"g-md-h2">Anaconda vs. Miniconda: Which one to install for =
Jupyter Notebook?</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">If you have 3 GB of space on your computer and want the=
 most straightforward installation, install Anaconda. Scroll to the Windows=
 Anaconda or Mac Anaconda section below.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">If you do not have 3 GB of space available or you want =
to save space and don=E2=80=99t mind doing some manual work, install Minico=
nda. Scroll to Windows Miniconda or Mac Miniconda</p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-installing-jupyter-notebook-using-anaconda-on-windows" cl=
ass=3D"g-md-h2">Installing Jupyter Notebook using Anaconda on Windows</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You will need to know what System type (number of bits)=
 you have before downloading the package (for more on bits, <a target=3D"_b=
lank" href=3D"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/32-bit-and-64-bit=
-windows-frequently-asked-questions-c6ca9541-8dce-4d48-0415-94a3faa2e13d" c=
lass=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">see her=
e</a>). If you are unsure, let=E2=80=99s check! </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><strong class=3D"g-md-strong">On Windows 10 and Windows=
 8.1:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"g-md-ol">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Select the Start button, then select Settings &gt; Sy=
stem &gt; About.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">At the right, under Device specifications, see System=
 type.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><strong class=3D"g-md-strong">On Windows 7:</strong></p=
>
<ol class=3D"g-md-ol">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Select the Start button, right-click Computer, and th=
en select Properties.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Under System, see the System type.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Screenshot of Windows device specifications=
 where system type is '64-bit operating system, x64-based processor'" class=
=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-scienc=
e-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/windows-system.PNG"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Go to the <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.anac=
onda.com/products/individual#Downloads" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-Ancho=
rBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Anaconda Downloads page</a> and download =
the appropriate version of Anaconda (32- or 64-bit Graphical Installer) </p=
>
<ol class=3D"g-md-ol">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Double click on the <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">.ex=
e</strong> file and click <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Install</kbd>. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Read and agree to the licensing terms.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Select if you want to install for =E2=80=98Just Me=E2=
=80=99 or =E2=80=98All Users=E2=80=99. If you are installing for =E2=80=98A=
ll Users=E2=80=99, you must have Administrator privileges.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">You will be prompted to select the installation locat=
ion. By default, Anaconda should try to install in your home directory. We =
recommend accepting this default. Click <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Install</kb=
d>.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">You will be asked if you want to add Anaconda to your=
 PATH environment variable. Do not add Anaconda to the PATH because it can =
interfere with other software. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">You will be asked if you want Anaconda to be your def=
ault version of Python. We recommend =E2=80=98Yes=E2=80=99. There are some =
rare instances where you might not make Anaconda the default version, but t=
hey are beyond the scope of this article.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Click the <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Install</kbd> butto=
n.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Go ahead and finish the installation.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Now, you can verify your installation. Go to the Window=
s Start menu and search for =E2=80=98Anaconda Navigator=E2=80=99 (not the A=
naconda Prompt). </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"anaconda navigator icon" class=3D"g-md-img"=
 src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-science-career-path=
/getting-started-off-platform/navigator-icon.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">If it appears, it is installed. Congratulations! </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Double-click on it, and the Anaconda Navigator window s=
hould appear. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Anaconda navigator prompt with menu of 'Hom=
e,' 'Environments,' 'Learning,' and 'Community' are listed. In Home, a few =
applications are visible, including JupyterLab and Jupyter Notebook." class=
=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-scienc=
e-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/anacondanavigator.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Your application screen may look slightly different fro=
m this one, but that is ok. Click the <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Launch</kbd> =
button under Jupyter Notebook. A Jupyter Notebook interface will appear in =
your default browser. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Jupyter Notebook file directory" class=3D"g=
-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-science-car=
eer-path/getting-started-off-platform/jupyter-directory-browser.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">An Anaconda Prompt might also open and display a URL. I=
f it does, do not close it until you are done working with Jupyter Notebook=
. If it does not appear, don=E2=80=99t worry - this has to do with your ope=
rating system and will not affect Jupyter Notebook=E2=80=99s performance. <=
/p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Congratulations!! You are ready to move on to the next =
article and <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article=
/setting-up-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14v=
pv2g0">get started using Jupyter Notebook</a>! </p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-installing-jupyter-notebook-using-miniconda-on-windows" c=
lass=3D"g-md-h2">Installing Jupyter Notebook using Miniconda on Windows</h2=
>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Go to the <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://docs.con=
da.io/en/latest/miniconda.html#windows-installers" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r=
92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Miniconda Downloads page</a>. =
Download the appropriate (32- or 64-bit) Python 3.X version of Miniconda. <=
/p>
<ol class=3D"g-md-ol">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Double click on the .exe file and click <kbd class=3D=
"g-md-kbd">Install</kbd>. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Read and agree to the licensing terms.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Select if you want to install for =E2=80=98Just Me=E2=
=80=99 or =E2=80=98All Users=E2=80=99. If you are installing for =E2=80=98A=
ll Users=E2=80=99, you must have Administrator privileges.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">You will be prompted to select the installation locat=
ion. By default, Anaconda should try to install in your home directory. We =
recommend accepting this default. Click <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Install</kb=
d>.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">You will be asked if you want to add Anaconda to your=
 PATH environment variable. Do not add Anaconda to the PATH because it can =
interfere with other software. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">You will be asked if you want Anaconda to be your def=
ault version of Python. We recommend =E2=80=98Yes=E2=80=99. There are some =
rare instances where you might not make Anaconda the default version, but t=
hey are beyond the scope of this article.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Click the <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Install</kbd> butto=
n.</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"heading-verify-miniconda-installation" class=3D"g-md-h3">Verify M=
iniconda installation</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">First, let=E2=80=99s verify that Miniconda was installe=
d. We will use the <code class=3D"g-md-code">Anaconda Prompt (miniconda3)</=
code> Go to the Start Menu and search for the Anaconda Prompt. Anaconda Pro=
mpt is the Command Line Interface (CLI) we will use with Miniconda (<a targ=
et=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/courses/learn-the-command-=
line/articles/command-line-setup" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase =
e14vpv2g0">more about the Command Line</a>). In the shell, type:</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"plaintext" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span class=3D=
"mtk1">conda --version</span></span><br><span><span></span></span><br></div=
></code></pre></pre>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Anaconda Prompt showing conda version 4.9.2=
" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data=
-science-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/windows-anaconda-version.=
PNG"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">A number should be returned. This is the version number=
 of conda that you have installed.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Now, we need to install a few key packages. In the Anac=
onda Prompt, type</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"plaintext" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span class=3D=
"mtk1">conda install jupyter</span></span><br><span><span></span></span><br=
></div></code></pre></pre>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">When prompted with =E2=80=98Proceed ([y]/n)?=E2=80=99 t=
ype <code class=3D"g-md-code">y</code></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"screenshot of terminal to conda install jup=
yter in which the user is asked whether to proceed with updating packages c=
a-certificates, certify, and openssl" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://sta=
tic-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-science-career-path/getting-started-of=
f-platform/windows-install-jupyter.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Once the installation completes, in the Anaconda Prompt=
, type:</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"plaintext" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span class=3D=
"mtk1">jupyter notebook</span></span><br><span><span></span></span><br></di=
v></code></pre></pre>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">A Jupyter Notebook interface will appear in your defaul=
t browser. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Jupyter Notebook file directory" class=3D"g=
-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-science-car=
eer-path/getting-started-off-platform/jupyter-directory-browser.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">An Anaconda Prompt might also open and display a URL. I=
f it does, do not close it until you are done working with Jupyter Notebook=
. If it does not appear, don=E2=80=99t worry =E2=80=94 this has to do with =
your operating system and will not affect Jupyter Notebook=E2=80=99s perfor=
mance.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"terminal showing Jupyter Notebook running w=
ith possible localhost urls" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-asset=
s.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-science-career-path/getting-started-off-platfor=
m/windows-jupyter-terminal-running.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-install-additional-python-packages" class=3D"g-md-h3">Ins=
tall additional Python packages</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Let=E2=80=99s install a few packages to get you started=
 working with data in Jupyter Notebook. These are all Python packages, so w=
e will use <code class=3D"g-md-code">pip</code> instead of <code class=3D"g=
-md-code">conda</code> to install them. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">We will load:</p>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://pandas.pydata.or=
g/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">pa=
ndas</a> for working with DataFrames.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://scikit-learn.org=
/stable/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopen=
er">scikit-learn</a> for machine learning.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://matplotlib.org/"=
 class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Matpl=
otlib</a> for visualizations.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://seaborn.pydata.o=
rg/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">s=
eaborn</a> for statistical visualizations.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.nltk.org/" c=
lass=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">NLTK</a=
> for text analysis.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://spacy.io/" class=
=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">spaCy</a> f=
or more text analysis.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Note that some of these packages depend on other packag=
es. For example, scikit-learn requires <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https:/=
/numpy.org/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noo=
pener">NumPy</a> (among others). Package managers (like pip) automatically =
find all the dependencies and install them for you. So when you install sci=
kit learn, pip automatically installs NumPy and any other dependencies scik=
it-learn needs. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Open a new Anaconda Prompt and type the following comma=
nds (hit =E2=80=98Enter=E2=80=99 after each row):</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"plaintext" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span class=3D=
"mtk1">pip install pandas</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">pip i=
nstall scikit-learn</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">pip install=
 matplotlib</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">pip install seaborn=
</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">pip install nltk</span></span>=
<br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">pip install beautifulsoup4</span></span><br>=
<span><span></span></span><br></div></code></pre></pre>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can check to be sure these are all installed by sta=
rting Python in your Anaconda Prompt. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">On a new line, type <code class=3D"g-md-code">python</c=
ode></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">The header will change to be <code class=3D"g-md-code">=
&gt;&gt;&gt;</code>:</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"terminal showing python version =E2=80=9CPy=
thon 3.8.5=E2=80=9D" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.codeca=
demy.com/Paths/data-science-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/window=
s-terminal-python%20type.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can import each package on a separate line or take =
a shortcut and import them all at once. Type:</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"AI Academy by RiWoT-python" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span =
class=3D"mtk12">import</span><span class=3D"mtk1"> </span><span class=3D"mt=
k9">pandas</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk12">import</span><span =
class=3D"mtk1"> </span><span class=3D"mtk9">sklearn</span></span><br><span>=
