<h3 id=3D"heading-install-additional-python-packages-1" class=3D"g-md-h3">I=
nstall additional Python packages</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Let=E2=80=99s install a few packages to get you started=
 working with data in Jupyter Notebook. These are all Python packages, so w=
e will use <code class=3D"g-md-code">pip</code> instead of <code class=3D"g=
-md-code">conda</code> to install them. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">We will load:</p>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://pandas.pydata.or=
g/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">pa=
ndas</a> for working with DataFrames.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://scikit-learn.org=
/stable/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopen=
er">scikit-learn</a> for machine learning.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://matplotlib.org/"=
 class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Matpl=
otlib</a> for visualizations.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://seaborn.pydata.o=
rg/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">s=
eaborn</a> for statistical visualizations.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.nltk.org/" c=
lass=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">NLTK</a=
> for text analysis.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://spacy.io/" class=
=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">spaCy</a> f=
or more text analysis.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Note that some of these packages depend on other packag=
es. For example, scikit-learn requires <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https:/=
/numpy.org/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noo=
pener">NumPy</a> (among other packages). Package managers (like pip) automa=
tically find all the dependencies and install them for you. So when you ins=
tall scikit-learn, pip automatically installs NumPy, and any other dependen=
cies scikit-learn needs.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Open a new BASH or zsh terminal and type the following =
commands:</p>
